      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "MelonLoader is the most common one for Unity games to load mods into.\nI know this, I use it on NeosVR only.\nThey could just ban the user on launch if MelonLoader files are found, or they could make the VRChat folder be verified and checked every few launches for mods.\nAgain, ban or warn user if mods are found, and delete mods.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-27T12:20:51.918Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Mod usage hasn't been dwindling. As a matter of fact, it's become more rampant.\nI notice a lot of people on VRChat use mods, even though it's against the community guidelines for VRChat. In theory, people would get punished for modifying the app, but the reality is, most people don't.\nThere isn't any method that VRChat uses, at least to my knowledge, to punish people who modify the app. Sure, there's the report button and occasionally, just blatant malicious behavior, but it doesn't seem like enough effort is put into ensuring that mod use isn't happening. This is one of the few reasons that mod usage is still happening within this community.\nAn anti-cheat, however, could change this issue. It may even be needed at this point to ensure that people don't use mods, and possibly even enforce some other rules.\nI don't know how anti-cheat engines work, or if it's even possible, but it's still a suggestion to try to find some sort of solution.",
